  "headline": "Indonesian Agency Monitors Seismic Activity In NTT And Maluku",
  "seoTitle": "Seismic Activity Monitored in NTT and Maluku",
  "metaDescription": "BMKG monitors ongoing aftershocks in NTT following a magnitude 5.8 earthquake as the region continues to track seismic activity in Maluku.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "A magnitude 5.8 earthquake struck the Manggarai Timur region of Nusa Tenggara Timur on November 18, 2026.",
    "The Meteorology, Climatology, and Geophysics Agency (BMKG) reported 17 aftershocks within one hour and confirmed no tsunami risk.",
    "Authorities continue to monitor seismic developments in NTT alongside recovery efforts following a recent magnitude 7.1 event in Maluku."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian Meteorology, Climatology, and Geophysics Agency (BMKG) is currently overseeing seismic activity across multiple regions. Following a recent magnitude 7.1 earthquake in Maluku that caused building damage, a new magnitude 5.8 seismic event occurred in Manggarai Timur, East Nusa Tenggara (NTT), on November 18, 2026. BMKG attributed the latest NTT earthquake to the Flores Back-arc Thrust. While the agency confirmed the event posed no tsunami threat, officials recorded at least 17 aftershocks in the hour following the initial tremor. Experts are actively monitoring the stability of the fault zones in both the Maluku and NTT regions to provide updates to the public. Meanwhile, emergency assessments are ongoing in Maluku to address infrastructure damage reported after the earlier, larger magnitude seismic event occurred in the Banda Sea.",
